==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|de|laßen||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gmw-pro|gem-pro|inh=2}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|lāzen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|lāzan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*lātan|t=to let, allow}}, whence English {{m|en|let}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|[ˈlasn̩]|[ˈlasən]}}
* {{audio|de|De-lassen.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-lassen.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|lassen<lässt#ließ,gelassen:lassen[with an infinitive]>}}

# {{lb|de|transitive|with an infinitive|past participle: “[[lassen]]”}} to [[allow]]; to [[permit]]; to [[let]]
#: {{uxi|de|lasset alle Hoffnung fahren|abandon all hope}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|with an infinitive|past participle: “[[lassen]]”}} to [[have]] someone (do something); to have (something done); to [[make]] (something happen); to [[cause]] (something to be done)
#: {{ux|de|Wir haben neue Schränke für die Küche machen '''lassen'''.|We '''had''' new cabinets made for the kitchen.}}
#: {{ux|de|Hast du dir die Haare schneiden lassen?|Did you '''get''' your hair cut?}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|past participle: “[[gelassen]]”}} to [[let]] remain, to [[leave]] (in a certain state)
#: {{ux|de|Mir ist es lieber, meine Haare grau zu '''lassen'''.|I prefer to '''leave''' my hair grey.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|past participle: “[[gelassen]]”}} to [[stop]] (something); to [[quit]]; to [[refrain]] from; to [[help]] doing (something)
# {{lb|de|intransitive|past participle: “[[gelassen]]”}} to [[cease]]; to [[desist]]

====Usage notes====
* Note that the English phrases "to ''let'' someone do something" and "to ''make'' someone do something" both translate into German as ''jemanden etwas tun lassen''. In order to avoid ambiguity, "to let" can be expressed as ''jemandem [[erlauben]], etwas zu tun'' or ''[[zulassen]], dass jemand etwas tut'', while "to make" can be expressed as ''jemanden dazu [[bringen]], etwas zu tun'' or ''dafür [[sorgen]], dass jemand etwas tut''.
* In perfect tenses, ''lassen'' + infinitive takes a double-infinitive construction, i.e. both verbs are in the infinitive: ''Ich habe mir die Haare <u>schneiden lassen</u>.'' (“I’ve had my hair cut.”). However, colloquially, ''gelassen'' may also be used.

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj|lassen<lässt#ließ,gelassen:lassen[with an infinitive]>}}
Some forms are missing in the above table, e.g.
* imperative plural: {{m|de|lasset}}
Traditionally ''ß'' is used in several places, e.g.:
* {{m|de|läßt}} instead of {{m|de|lässt}}
* {{m|de|laßt}} instead of {{m|de|lasst}}

